## Describe the bug

Sign-in via the built-in GitHub OAuth provider fails with the following error in the Langfuse web container logs:

```
[next-auth][error][OAUTH_CALLBACK_ERROR]
https://next-auth.js.org/errors#oauth_callback_error issuer must be configured on the issuer {
  error: Error [OAuthCallbackError]: issuer must be configured on the issuer
  ...
  providerId: 'github',
  message: 'issuer must be configured on the issuer'
}
```

The browser is redirected to the sign-in page showing `OAuthCallback` / "Contact support if this error is unexpected."

## Root cause

GitHub recently started returning an `iss` parameter in OAuth callback responses, implementing [RFC 9207 (OAuth 2.0 Authorization Server Issuer Identification)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9207). The parameter value is `https://github.com/login/oauth`.

`openid-client` (used by NextAuth v4) performs the following check when `iss` is present in the callback:

```
if params.iss is present:
    if client.issuer.metadata.issuer is empty:
        throw "issuer must be configured on the issuer"
    if params.iss != client.issuer.metadata.issuer:
        throw "iss mismatch"
```

Because Langfuse's `GitHubProvider` configuration in `web/src/server/auth.ts` does **not** set an `issuer`, `openid-client` throws `issuer must be configured on the issuer` as soon as GitHub includes `iss`:

```ts
// web/src/server/auth.ts
if (env.AUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID && env.AUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET)
  staticProviders.push(
    GitHubProvider({
      clientId: env.AUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID,
      clientSecret: env.AUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET,
      allowDangerousEmailAccountLinking:
        env.AUTH_GITHUB_ALLOW_ACCOUNT_LINKING === "true",
      client: {
        token_endpoint_auth_method: env.AUTH_GITHUB_CLIENT_AUTH_METHOD,
      },
      ...(env.AUTH_GITHUB_CHECKS ? { checks: env.AUTH_GITHUB_CHECKS } : {}),
      // no `issuer` set ← this is the problem
    }),
  );
```

