### Problem

Image preview does not render when a CDN returns `Content-Type: application/octet-stream` instead of `image/*`.

Many CDNs and S3 buckets serve image files with `application/octet-stream` when Content-Type metadata is not explicitly set at upload time. Browsers can render these images without issue via `<img>` tags, but `isImageContent()` in Langfuse rejects them server-side.

### Current behavior

In [`web/src/server/api/routers/utilities.ts`](https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/blob/main/web/src/server/api/routers/utilities.ts), `isImageContent` strictly requires `Content-Type` to start with `image/`:

```typescript
const isImageContent = (response: Response): boolean => {
  const contentType = response.headers.get("content-type");
  return !!contentType && contentType.startsWith("image/");
};
```

For non-S3 image URLs (e.g., CloudFront), `isValidImageUrl` falls through to a `HEAD` request. If the response returns `application/octet-stream`, `isImageContent` returns `false` and the preview is blocked — even though the URL points to a valid image.

### Expected behavior

When `Content-Type` is `application/octet-stream`, Langfuse should fall back to a URL pathname extension check (`.webp`, `.jpg`, `.png`, etc.) before rejecting the image.

### Suggested fix

```typescript
const IMAGE_EXTENSIONS = /\.(jpe?g|png|gif|webp|svg|bmp|ico|avif|tiff?)$/i;

// In isValidImageUrl, after isImageContent returns false:
const contentType = response.headers.get("content-type");
if (contentType === "application/octet-stream") {
  const pathname = new URL(url).pathname;
  return IMAGE_EXTENSIONS.test(pathname);
}
```

### To reproduce

1. Send a trace containing an image URL served by a CDN that returns `Content-Type: application/octet-stream`
2. Open the trace in Langfuse UI
3. Image preview does not render
4. Opening the same URL directly in the browser displays the image correctly

